WEBVTT

00:58:58.517 --> 00:59:01.560
"Well, what would it look like
if people were to figure it out?

00:59:01.584 --> 00:59:03.610
Does that have to be done in a giant leap?

00:59:03.634 --> 00:59:04.923
Can it be done piecemeal?

00:59:04.947 --> 00:59:06.965
Who are the people who might do that?"

00:59:06.989 --> 00:59:10.040
Maybe those people should be
on the front page of the newspaper

00:59:10.064 --> 00:59:11.233
from time to time.

00:59:11.257 --> 00:59:14.042
They often are not.
They're just ignored or laughed at.

00:59:14.066 --> 00:59:16.417
DB: Right, and one of the good
moments for me was,

00:59:16.441 --> 00:59:18.396
I looked back through the social science

00:59:18.420 --> 00:59:21.763
and the big public intellectual literature
of the past hundred years,

00:59:21.787 --> 00:59:24.111
and in every decade,
people were too pessimistic.

00:59:24.135 --> 00:59:27.210
There was always "the decline of this"
and "the decline of that,"

00:59:27.234 --> 00:59:29.298
and "the end of this"
and "the end of that."

00:59:29.322 --> 00:59:31.861
And you look back, they were
complaining in the 1950s.